the first thing you notice is that there are words that you know how to say, and words that you do not know how to say, and a vast, indescribable void between them. and you cannot say anything at all without saying both the one that you know how to say and the one that you do not know how to say, because the one that you do not know how to say is the way of saying the one that you know how to say.

